  "rationale": {
    "bootPathUse": "no member below is referenced by the guest boot path; sudo and passwd appear only as package names in the dependency closure",
    "danglingSymlinks": "a symlink whose target is absent is not an error the closure can fix; masking units point at /dev/null on purpose and conffile targets come from control.tar, which the frozen builder never reads",
    "derivedUsrmergeSymlinks": "base-files is not in this closure, so no package ships the merged-/usr symlinks; the sealed lock derives /lib because 347 binaries name their ELF interpreter under it, but stops there, and the kernel hands PID 1 to /sbin/init. /bin completes the same canonical merged-/usr layout that every path in the closure already assumes. Adding these two rows does not supply a shell -- see boundaries.shellAbsence. /lib64 is not added because arm64 does not use it and nothing in the closure references it.",
    "ruleSatisfied": "native-shadow-boot-image-builder-authority-arm64-v1.json determinism.ownership = root:root-only",
    "usrmerge": "Ubuntu 24.04 is merged-/usr and the sealed lock already derives /lib -> usr/lib, so lib/x and usr/lib/x name one file; relocating moves paths and never decides which of two colliding members wins",
    "why": "the sealed image rule already requires root:root-only; the frozen builder refuses rather than silently rewriting, so the rewrite is enumerated here instead"
  },
